sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Nexus and Rift access flow
    accDescr: An operator configures Nexus and creates a Rift with one room. The operator creates or recovers a managed frame, Rift attaches it only after policy, descriptor, and ACL checks, Nexus compiles projections, and Rift applies them to room assets. ACL revisions drain Rift gates before refreshing impacted projections.

    actor Agent as Operator / agent
    participant Nexus
    participant Policy as Frame managers + ACL
    participant Rift
    participant Room as RiftSpace
    participant Runtime as AethericFrame runtime

    rect rgb(231,247,250)
        Agent->>Nexus: configure + enable
        Agent->>Nexus: create_rift(room posture)
        Nexus->>Rift: construct + register
        Rift->>Room: create one primary room
    end
    rect rgb(244,234,255)
        Agent->>Nexus: create/get managed frame
        Nexus->>Runtime: Spellbook.conjure(dynamic=True)
        Runtime-->>Agent: rooted Conduit
        Agent->>Rift: create_frame_link(frame)
        Rift->>Nexus: validate target policy
        Nexus->>Policy: require descriptor + frame ACL
        Policy-->>Nexus: selected contracts
        Nexus-->>Rift: compiled projection set
        Rift->>Room: apply viewer + command projections
    end
    rect rgb(234,247,239)
        Agent->>Room: inspect · bind target · command
        Room->>Rift: acquire RiftGate ticket
        Room->>Runtime: allowed operation
        Runtime-->>Room: current object / result
        Room-->>Agent: bounded response
    end
    rect rgb(255,240,232)
        Policy->>Nexus: ACL family revision
        Nexus->>Rift: disable gate + drain
        Nexus->>Policy: compile changed-frame subset
        Policy-->>Rift: refreshed projections
        Rift->>Room: merge + reapply assets
        Nexus->>Rift: reopen gate
    end
